DESCRIPTION:Organizer: Chicago Public Library\\nCost: free\\nAges: 0-60 mo
 nths\\nCategory: Storytime\\n\\nJoin a local TreeKeeper to get to know the
  trees in our South Shore neighborhood. Learn to identify common trees in 
 Chicago and learn about their unique qualities\, lineages and their relati
 onships to one another and why a diversity of species keeps our urban fore
 st resilient. You'll learn some basics of tree identification\, as well as
  how the trees in our neighborhood fit into the larger picture of evolutio
 n and ecology. Openlands TreeKeepers are a group of volunteer urban forest
  stewards that a\\n\\nMore info: https://chipublib.bibliocommons.com/event
 s/6a6a382df213992f00c7f195
LOCATION:South Shore\, 2505 E. 73rd St.\, Chicago\, IL 60649
