SUMMARY:Meet a Scientist: fan-Tusk-tic Dicynodonts
DTSTART;TZID=America/Chicago:20260821T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Chicago:20260821T130000
DTSTAMP:20260809T084319Z
UID:4b6a8f17baeb8323b294de81b1b0fccf@family-events-agent
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:museum,science,family,all_audiences
DESCRIPTION:Organizer: Field Museum - Events\\nCost: Included with admissi
 on\\nAges: All ages\\nCategory: Music & Dance\\n\\nDicynodonts are a remar
 kable group of ancient mammal relatives famous for being the first group t
 o evolve true tusks. Using paleohistology - the study of fossil tissues - 
 we can peer within dicynodont tusks to uncover a wealth of biological info
 rmation preserved inside. Join Ken Angielczyk and Kara Mia Ehler in the Sc
 ience Hub to microscopically explore fossilized tusks and reveal how these
  animals lived\, grew\, and adapted to their environment about 255 million
  years ago!\\n\\nMore info: https://www.fieldmuseum.org/our-events/meet-a-
 scientist/meet-a-scientist-fan-tusk-tic-dicynodonts
LOCATION:Field Museum\, 1400 S Lake Shore Dr\, Chicago\, IL 60605
URL:https://www.fieldmuseum.org/our-events/meet-a-scientist/meet-a-scienti
 st-fan-tusk-tic-dicynodonts
