CATEGORIES:storytime,library,baby,toddler,reading
DESCRIPTION:Organizer: Chicago Public Library\\nCost: free\\nAges: 0-60 mo
 nths\\nCategory: Play & Games\\n\\nMenopause is a natural transition that 
 is often misunderstood\, under-discussed\, and filled with conflicting inf
 ormation. This monthly series brings together experts\, advocates\, and re
 al women’s experiences to shed light on every stage of the journey. From
  hormones to mental health\, relationships to research\, each session offe
 rs practical tools\, evidence-based insight\, and space for honest convers
 ation. Together\, we’ll replace confusion with clarity\, and empower eac
 h other to navigate menopause w\\n\\nMore info: https://chipublib.biblioco
 mmons.com/events/697a4bfc834cbb3dea29e912
LOCATION:Sulzer Regional\, 4455 N. Lincoln Ave.\, Chicago\, IL 60625
URL:https://chipublib.bibliocommons.com/events/697a4bfc834cbb3dea29e912
